{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is what was wrong and what changed.\n\n### Problem\n`insert_index` behaved like `bisect_left`: it used `sorted_list[mid] < x` in the binary search, so equal values were inserted **before** existing runs of the same value. For `[1, 2, 2, 3]` and `x=2`, that returned `1` instead of `3`.\n\n### Fix\nThe comparison is now `sorted_list[mid] <= x`, which is the usual right-insertion rule (`bisect_right`): new equal values go **after** any existing equals. Non-equal cases are unchanged (e.g. `4` in `[1, 3, 5]` still yields index `2`).\n\n### Cleanup\n- Removed the stale `BUG` comment and the unused `old_insert_index` wrapper (nothing imported it).\n- Added a short docstring describing the contract.\n\n`tests/visible/test_bisect.py` passes. `rows.bisect_summary` still uses `insert_index` and now gets the correct insertion index for duplicate values."}]},"session_id":"8138ceb4-470f-4efa-885a-01344eb0b69a"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":41184,"duration_api_ms":41184,"is_error":false,"result":"Inspecting `repo/search.py` and how it's used across the codebase.\n\n\nFixing `insert_index` to use right insertion (after equal elements) and removing the unused legacy helper.\n\n\nHere is what was wrong and what changed.\n\n### Problem\n`insert_index` behaved like `bisect_left`: it used `sorted_list[mid] < x` in the binary search, so equal values were inserted **before** existing runs of the same value. For `[1, 2, 2, 3]` and `x=2`, that returned `1` instead of `3`.\n\n### Fix\nThe comparison is now `sorted_list[mid] <= x`, which is the usual right-insertion rule (`bisect_right`): new equal values go **after** any existing equals. Non-equal cases are unchanged (e.g. `4` in `[1, 3, 5]` still yields index `2`).\n\n### Cleanup\n- Removed the stale `BUG` comment and the unused `old_insert_index` wrapper (nothing imported it).\n- Added a short docstring describing the contract.\n\n`tests/visible/test_bisect.py` passes. `rows.bisect_summary` still uses `insert_index` and now gets the correct insertion index for duplicate values.","session_id":"8138ceb4-470f-4efa-885a-01344eb0b69a","request_id":"73b81b6b-ce9d-408b-9091-08f9610207a2","usage":{"inputTokens":12516,"outputTokens":1600,"cacheReadTokens":77864,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
